```mdl
verdict F-3.1: The re-scan works, but no user-invocable "Refresh Folder" exists; refresh happens only through the directory watcher.
  status: partial
  evidence:
    [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/state/directory-watcher.ts#createDirectoryWatcher,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/state/state.ts#handleDirectoryRefresh]
  note: |
    `RefreshDirectory` is defined and handled, but no graph action or UI invokes it (grep finds no caller). The watcher
    (`watchImmediate`, recursive, 500 ms debounce) refreshes on create, remove and rename. Graph sync on state replacement is
    tested with a mock; the refresh path itself is not.
```

```mdl
verdict F-3.2: Open files are not closed, but their nodes go briefly to the pending state during a manual refresh.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/state/FileSystemManager.ts#refreshWorkspaceContent]
  note: |
    `refreshWorkspaceContent` evicts all docs before the async disk re-scan. The open node's data flips to `null`
    (`markdown-pending`) until `syncFromDisk` re-binds it through the xattr or filemap. If that lookup fails, a new Text object is
    created, so the open editor ends up on a different object. The watcher path (`handleDirectoryRefresh`) evicts after the scan,
    so the gap is shorter. No test.
```

