```mdl
verdict F-4.6: The order is stored in the settings space's `shared-spaces` Expando, the same array plugin-space uses.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/app-graph-builder.ts#workspaceRearrangeCache]
  note: |
    `onRearrange` is attached only if the shared order object already exists. It is cached for each workspace id in a module-level
    map that is never cleared, so it keeps the first `spacesOrder` object it saw (and survives plugin reloads). The spec says
    "personal space"; the code reads `AppSpace.getSettingsSpace`. No test.
```

```mdl
verdict F-5.1: The registered Markdown extension is a save-to-disk listener; the shared editor comes from emitting Text-typed nodes.
  status: diverged
  evidence:
    [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/markdown-extension.ts#extensionProvider,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/index.ts#Markdown]
  note: The outcome the requirement wants (same editor surface) holds, but not because of the extension. The `ExtensionProvider` is a `listener` that writes edits back to disk. Reword the requirement.
```

```mdl
verdict F-5.2: Text objects are created eagerly for every markdown file when a workspace is activated, not when a node is activated.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/capabilities/state/markdown-documents.ts#syncFromDisk]
  note: |
    `syncFromDisk` runs on open, on refresh and on startup restore. It restores Text through the xattr or filemap, or creates a new
    one for each file, before anything is opened. Disk wins on divergence (`updateText`). Large folders pay the full cost up front.
```

